body:
Hello everybody!
When i trying to use custom hasher (placed in my plugin's dir - ROOT_DIR/plugins/Codercms/Auth/LegacyPasswordHasher.php) in Auth component, i always getting error - Password hasher class "Legacy" was not found..
Code of file:

``` <?php
namespace Codercms\Auth;
use Cake\Auth\AbstractPasswordHasher;

class LegacyPasswordHasher extends AbstractPasswordHasher {

    public function hash($password) {
        return md5(md5($password));
    }

    public function check($password, $hashedPassword) {
        return $hashedPassword === $this->hash($password);
    }
}
```

Config in base plugin's controller:

``` <?php
 public $components = [
        'Auth' => [
            'loginAction' => [
                'plugin' => 'Codercms',
                'controller' => 'Members',
                'action' => 'login'
            ],
            'authenticate' => [
                'Codercms.Form' => [
                    'userModel' => 'Codercms.Members'
                    'passwordHasher' => 'Codercms.Legacy'
                ]
            ]
        ]
    ];
```

(ofc, i tried something like this:  'passwordHasher' => ['plugin' => 'Codercms', 'className' => 'Legacy' ])
So, i went to call stack last calling - it's PasswordHasherFactory::build (/vendor/cakephp/cakephp/src/Auth/PasswordHasherFactory.php).

``` <?php
public static function build($passwordHasher) {
        $config = [];
        if (is_string($passwordHasher)) {
            $class = $passwordHasher;
        } else {
            $class = $passwordHasher['className'];
            $config = $passwordHasher;
            unset($config['className']);
        }

        list($plugin, $class) = pluginSplit($class, true);

        $className = App::className($class, 'Auth', 'PasswordHasher');

        if (!class_exists($className)) {
            throw new \RuntimeException(sprintf('Password hasher class "%s" was not found.', $class));
        }

        $hasher = new $className($config);
        if (!($hasher instanceof AbstractPasswordHasher)) {
            throw new \RuntimeException('Password hasher must extend AbstractPasswordHasher class.');
        }

        return $hasher;
    }
```

The bug is here, it always using default namespace (App) from ROOT_DIR/config/app.php config.
And it's cannot be changed or your cakephp will be ruined.

So, i just moved the custom password hasher to /vendor/cakephp/cakephp/src/Auth/, changed namespace from Codercms\Auth to Cake\Auth and removed prefix "Codercms." from config in base plugin's controller (it's value of "passwordHasher" field). After that all, custom password hasher work's fine.

P.S. Sorry for my English.
